# What never belongs in a Docker build context.
#
# All three Dockerfiles take the REPOSITORY ROOT as their context, because
# packages/core is a workspace dependency of every app. Without this file that
# context is the entire working tree — including every node_modules, every build
# output, and .env — and Coolify builds on the VM, so all of it is shipped to the
# daemon on every deploy.
#
# Four distinct failures are prevented here, in increasing order of nastiness.

# ── 1. Secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No Dockerfile copies .env today; they all copy explicit paths and none uses
# `COPY . .`. This is the guard for the day one of them does. A bot token and a
# MODEL_API_KEY committed into an image layer pushed to ECR cannot be undone by
# rebuilding — the only remedy is rotating the credentials.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── 2. Stale build output, which is the subtle one ────────────────────────────
# `COPY packages/core packages/core` is a directory copy, so it would bring the
# host's dist AND .tsbuildinfo into the build stage. `tsc --build` consults
# .tsbuildinfo to decide what needs recompiling; a stale one convinces it
# everything is current, so it skips the build and leaves the stale dist in the
# image. Core's exports resolve to dist, so that image then serves the PREVIOUS
# API without erroring — the same failure that had apps/agent passing against an
# outdated core, except inside a container whose logs are read through CloudWatch.
#
# The images build core themselves. Nothing compiled on the host should travel.
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.next
**/.next

# ── 3. Dependencies ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These directories exist for apps/agent, apps/worker and packages/core, so the
# directory copies above would pick them up. Under pnpm they are symlink farms
# pointing into node_modules/.pnpm, landing on top of the `pnpm install` the deps
# stage already ran. Best case dead weight; worst case a stale symlink shadows a
# correctly installed dependency and produces a resolution error that reproduces
# on no other machine. Each image installs from pnpm-lock.yaml instead.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store

# ── 4. Weight ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Coolify builds on the VM, where free memory is already a recorded risk for the
# Next.js production build. None of this is needed to build any image:
#   docs/hackathon-ideas.json   ~6.6 MB
#   scripts/out/                the rendered transcript, ~834 KB, derived
docs
scripts/out
.git
.github
.codegraph

# Database dumps — the golden reset point is large and belongs nowhere near an image.
*.dump
*.pgdump
dumps
golden.sql

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
